# The FAST SET -- one representative case per tutorial FAMILY (declared
# 2026-09-07, task #84 slice 1).
#
# WHAT THIS IS.  `bin/runTests --fast` runs exactly these cases through the
# SAME per-case checks as the full sweep (NaN/inf guard, golden-master KPIs,
# anchor rows) and then four CONSERVATION gates, and answers, in seconds:
#
#     is any FAMILY of the corpus going dark?
#
# It is the rung BETWEEN the two that already existed.  `--witnesses` runs 15
# cases, one per EXECUTION CLASS, and answers "does each class still traverse
# the architecture?"; the full sweep runs ~590 items in 31-43 min and answers
# "did we break any historical case, and does every gate still hold?".
# Neither serves the question a builder actually asks after a slice.  Twelve
# architectural classes do not cover the corpus's SHAPE: an adsorber change, a
# psychrometrics change and a hydraulics change all pass `--witnesses`
# untouched, because none of those is an execution class.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS, measured.  On 2026-09-07, across one builder day, NINE full
# sweeps were run and FOUR of them were INTERMEDIATE -- run to find out
# whether the work was going well, not to authorise a commit.  That is ~140
# min of a 571-min day spent on the wrong rung of the ladder.
#
# THE DERIVATION.  A FAMILY is the directory a case's siblings share -- the
# case's own parent directory -- EXCEPT under `tutorials/plant/`, where each
# PLANT is a family (its sub-cases belong to it), because two plants share
# nothing but the folder they sit in.  So `tutorials/steady/flash` is one
# family, the flat `tutorials/ctrl` is ONE family of 20 case directories
# serving one binary, and `tutorials/plant/lithiumBrinePlant` is a family of
# its own.  Measured against the tree on 2026-09-07 by check_fastset:
#
#     families holding >= 1 case the suite walks                 57
#       - 1   plant/acetonePlant, EXCLUDED below and named there
#       + 2   ctrl/ contributes 3 representatives, not 1
#       + 1   electrochem/ contributes 2 representatives, not 1
#       ---
#        59   lines in this file
#
# ctrl/ and electrochem/ are flat categories whose cases are one family by the
# rule above but several PHYSICS by any other reading, so each is given a few
# of its cheapest rather than one.  That is a judgement, made here, in review
# -- exactly as `tutorials/WITNESSES` makes its representativeness judgement.
#
# THE LIST IS DECLARED, AND ITS COMPLETENESS IS GATED.  Not derived ("the
# cheapest case per family" is not stable -- two complete runs of the same 598
# items on the same day measured 42.5 and 31.3 min, a 26 % spread, so a
# derived list would reshuffle between runs and nobody could review it or
# reason about what it covers).  Not hand-kept alone either: a hand-kept list
# goes stale SILENTLY the first time a family is added, and a missing case
# does not fail -- it just stops running, which is the check_true_ions failure
# shape.  So `bin/curate/check_fastset.py` recomputes the family set from the
# tree the same way bin/runTests gathers cases and REFUSES when a walked
# family has no line here.
#
# THE ONE FAMILY WITH NO REPRESENTATIVE, declared rather than silent:
#
# EXCLUDED  tutorials/plant/ammonia02_full_plant  its golden carries 126 rows the
#           first-law work of 2026-09-07 moved and Vitor has not re-recorded;
#           walking it here would make --fast red on a KNOWN DEBT instead of on
#           a regression, which is how a tier teaches people to ignore it.  The
#           full sweep meets the case and reports the same rows.  This line
#           EXPIRES the day those goldens are re-recorded -- put the case back.
# EXCLUDED  tutorials/plant/acetonePlant  39.97 s -- over the 3 s per-case cap this list is built to; the tier is checked by the full sweep instead
#
# THE FOUR CONSERVATION GATES, and why those four.  A golden pins what a run
# PRINTS, so a stable wrong answer passes by construction: the spray dryer of
# 2026-09-04 created 2948 kg/h of water on a case the suite PASSED.
# Conservation is the class of defect no golden can see, so `--fast` runs
# mass-closure, element-balance, closure-ledger-pinned and energy-boundary-
# pinned over the cases it just ran -- measured at 0.97 s together on a run
# that has the case outputs in hand, which is free.  `charge-balance` (2.45 s)
# and `stream-transport` (13.1 s) are NOT free at this tier and stay out; they
# are the full sweep's.
#
# THIS IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR THE FULL SWEEP and authorises no commit; the
# flag says so in its own verdict line rather than leaving a reader to
# remember it.  It runs NO other gate, no golden-manifest check, no build-
# freshness check and no `--record` anything.
#
# EACH LINE: one case path, relative to the repository root.  The FAMILY is
# NOT written here -- it is the path's own parent, and writing it would be a
# second home for a fact the path already carries.  Gate: check_fastset
# (existence, walked, uniqueness, and the completeness arm check_witness_tier
# deliberately does not have).

